functions: The functions of templates and expressions.

A template calls a function with its arguments after it, separated by
spaces: {{ join .vars.names ", " }}. An expression calls it with
parentheses: join(vars.names, ", "). The type column below tells where
a function works.

Templates also have the actions of Go's text/template: if, else, range,
with, define, template, block, break, and continue, and the variables
$x := value. In an expression, pred is a predicate: an expression that
reads the element as #, or a key of a map element as .name, such as
filter(vars.users, .uid >= 1000).

Keys:
  abs            expression            -  abs(n): the absolute value of the number n.
  all            expression            -  all(list, pred): true when pred is true for each element.
  and            template              -  and x y: the first empty argument, or the last argument.
  any            expression            -  any(list, pred): true when pred is true for at least one element.
  bitand         expression            -  bitand(a, b): the bitwise AND of two integers.
  bitnand        expression            -  bitnand(a, b): the bitwise AND NOT of two integers.
  bitnot         expression            -  bitnot(a): the bitwise NOT of an integer.
  bitor          expression            -  bitor(a, b): the bitwise OR of two integers.
  bitshl         expression            -  bitshl(a, n): a shifted left by n bits.
  bitshr         expression            -  bitshr(a, n): a shifted right by n bits, with its sign.
  bitushr        expression            -  bitushr(a, n): a shifted right by n bits, without its sign.
  bitxor         expression            -  bitxor(a, b): the bitwise XOR of two integers.
  call           template              -  call f args: the result of the function f.
  ceil           expression            -  ceil(n): n rounded up to an integer value.
  concat         expression            -  concat(a, b, ...): the lists joined into one list.
  count          expression            -  count(list, pred): the number of elements for which pred is true.
  date           expression            -  date(s), date(s, layout), or date(s, layout, zone): the time in the text s, such as date("2026-10-30").
  duration       expression            -  duration(s): the duration in the text s, such as duration("1h30m").
  eq             template              -  eq a b: true when a equals b.
  filter         expression            -  filter(list, pred): the elements for which pred is true: filter(match("all"), .name != host.name).
  find           expression            -  find(list, pred): the first element for which pred is true, or nil.
  findIndex      expression            -  findIndex(list, pred): the index of the first element for which pred is true, or -1.
  findLast       expression            -  findLast(list, pred): the last element for which pred is true, or nil.
  findLastIndex  expression            -  findLastIndex(list, pred): the index of the last element for which pred is true, or -1.
  first          expression            -  first(list): the first element, or nil for an empty list.
  flatten        expression            -  flatten(list): the elements of the list and of its nested lists, in one list.
  float          expression            -  float(v): the number or the text v as a float.
  floor          expression            -  floor(n): n rounded down to an integer value.
  fromBase64     expression            -  fromBase64(s): the text that the base64 text s encodes.
  fromJSON       expression            -  fromJSON(s): the value of the JSON text s.
  fromPairs      expression            -  fromPairs(list): a map from a list of [key, value] pairs.
  ge             template              -  ge a b: true when a >= b.
  get            template, expression  -  get m key, or get(m, key): the value of key in the map m, or nothing when m has no such key.
  groupBy        expression            -  groupBy(list, pred): a map from each result of pred to the list of elements that give it.
  gt             template              -  gt a b: true when a > b.
  has            template              -  has list v: true when list contains v.
  hasPrefix      expression            -  hasPrefix(s, prefix): true when s starts with prefix.
  hasSuffix      expression            -  hasSuffix(s, suffix): true when s ends with suffix.
  html           template              -  html s: s with the special characters of HTML escaped.
  index          template              -  index x k: the element of the map or the list x at the key or the index k.
  indexOf        expression            -  indexOf(s, sub): the index of the first sub in s, or -1.
  int            expression            -  int(v): the number or the text v as an integer: int("8080").
  join           template, expression  -  join list sep, or join(list, sep): the elements of list joined with sep.
  js             template              -  js s: s escaped for a JavaScript string.
  json           template, expression  -  json v, or json(v): v as JSON on one line.
  keys           expression            -  keys(m): the keys of the map m, in sorted order.
  last           expression            -  last(list): the last element, or nil for an empty list.
  lastIndexOf    expression            -  lastIndexOf(s, sub): the index of the last sub in s, or -1.
  le             template              -  le a b: true when a <= b.
  len            template, expression  -  len x, or len(x): the length of a string, a list, or a map.
  lower          expression            -  lower(s): s in lower case.
  lt             template              -  lt a b: true when a < b.
  map            expression            -  map(list, pred): the result of pred for each element: map(vars.users, .name).
  match          expression            -  match(pattern): the hosts that match the host pattern, each with name, short, address, groups, and vars, as host has.
  max            expression            -  max(a, b, ...), or max(list): the largest number.
  mean           expression            -  mean(list): the average of the numbers.
  median         expression            -  median(list): the median of the numbers.
  min            expression            -  min(a, b, ...), or min(list): the smallest number.
  ne             template              -  ne a b: true when a does not equal b.
  none           expression            -  none(list, pred): true when pred is false for each element.
  not            template              -  not x: true when x is empty or false.
  one            expression            -  one(list, pred): true when pred is true for exactly one element.
  or             template              -  or x y: the first argument that is not empty, or the last argument.
  print          template              -  print args: the arguments as text, as Go's fmt.Sprint gives them.
  printf         template              -  printf format args: the arguments formatted as Go's fmt.Sprintf does: {{ printf "%05d" .vars.uid }}.
  println        template              -  println args: the arguments as text, with spaces between them and a newline at the end.
  quote          template, expression  -  quote s, or quote(s): s in single quotes for sh, each ' as '\''.
  reduce         expression            -  reduce(list, pred, initial): one value from all elements.
  repeat         expression            -  repeat(s, n): s n times.
  replace        expression            -  replace(s, old, new): s with each old replaced by new.
  reverse        expression            -  reverse(list): the elements in reverse order.
  round          expression            -  round(n): n rounded to the nearest integer value.
  slice          template              -  slice x i j: the part of the string or the list x from the index i up to j.
  sort           expression            -  sort(list), or sort(list, "desc"): the elements in ascending or descending order.
  sortBy         expression            -  sortBy(list, pred), or sortBy(list, pred, "desc"): the elements in the order of the results of pred: sortBy(vars.users, .uid).
  split          expression            -  split(s, sep), or split(s, sep, n): the parts of s between each sep.
  splitAfter     expression            -  splitAfter(s, sep), or splitAfter(s, sep, n): the parts of s after each sep, each with sep at its end.
  sqlquote       template, expression  -  sqlquote s, or sqlquote(s): s as a MariaDB string literal: in single quotes, each ' as '', each \ as \\.
  string         expression            -  string(v): v as text: string(8080) is "8080".
  sum            expression            -  sum(list), or sum(list, pred): the sum of the numbers, or of the results of pred.
  take           expression            -  take(list, n): the first n elements.
  timezone       expression            -  timezone(name): the time zone name, such as "Europe/Berlin", for the In method of a date.
  title          template              -  title s: s with the first letter of each word in upper case.
  toBase64       expression            -  toBase64(s): s in base64.
  toPairs        expression            -  toPairs(m): the [key, value] pairs of the map m, in sorted key order.
  trim           expression            -  trim(s), or trim(s, chars): s without white space, or without the characters in chars, at both ends.
  trimPrefix     expression            -  trimPrefix(s, prefix): s without prefix at its start.
  trimSuffix     expression            -  trimSuffix(s, suffix): s without suffix at its end.
  type           expression            -  type(v): the type of v as text: nil, bool, int, float, string, array, map, time.Time for a date, or time.Duration.
  uniq           expression            -  uniq(list): the elements without repeats, in their first order.
  upper          expression            -  upper(s): s in upper case.
  urlquery       template              -  urlquery s: s escaped for the query of a URL.
  values         expression            -  values(m): the values of the map m, in the order of its sorted keys.

Run "winch doc functions.<key>" for the full text of a key.
